      },
      "description": "On a far away terrestrial planet, there is a humanoid race with rabbit ears living on a peninsula named Alfau, they are called Alfaus. The Alfaus is a humanoid race with rabbit-like features, their height, skin, organs, and skeleton are all similar to humans, but they have a pair of iconic long rabbit ears and a furry, tape-measure-like rabbit tail, in addition, their legs are quite strong, and the structure and shape of their feet are also very suitable for high-speed running and jumping. Moreover, their fertility is significantly stronger than that of ordinary humans, and their sexual impulses are more frequent and intense. This series of biological characteristics combined with the enclosed geographical environment of the Alfau Peninsula made them the most densely populated race on their home planet, and created a unique social development history, social form, and social culture, known as the Alfau Civilization.\n\nIn the early stages of the development of the Alfau Civilization, the Alfau Peninsula fell into a highly intense civil war due to its large population and limited land. Only the tribes with eased internal conflicts, reasonable resource distribution, and population growth sufficient to offset war consumption were able to survive. So under the pressure of survival, Alfaus not only invented concepts such as professional bureaucracy, planned economy, and socialized upbringing far ahead of other races, but also formed systems and cultures that curb privilege, even those tribes where only a handful of bureaucrats had the opportunity to embezzle a handful of grain were filtered out by war and famine. After the extinction of over half of the entire race, the civil war finally came to an end, and a civilization that could never escape from the 'primitive society' was born, but for people living in the future, its social form is too familiar: A 'primitive society' with a professional bureaucratic system responsible for the clan assembly, population and economic planning with rational guidance and universal social welfare and public upbringing. However, whether limited by technology and productivity levels, or by the supervisory ability of clan members, most administrative management and political and economic activities were confined to a certain region, with no interference between regions, and the entire society maintained a highly autonomous state based on clan communes.\n\nThe secretaries were born in such a society, they are Alfaus clones created using relics from prehistoric civilization, through the combination of genetic engineering and implants, they are more agile, stronger, and smarter than ordinary Alfaus, while also having graceful bodies and full of idealism and dedication. They are able to communicate with each other in spirit, share senses, and even replace their bodies to achieve eternal life through prehistoric technologies with unknown principles. The specific process of the birth of this clone race is no longer traceable. In Alfaus' memories today, secretaries initially served as bureaucrats of worker clans living in the port cities of the Alfau Peninsula, and later took over the already limited national administrative functions. In the interstellar era, most clans still insist on managing their own internal affairs, Only regard secretaries as convenient tools for participating in national politics and communicating with other clans. Only in rimworlds, hive cities and military units do secretaries undertake more functions. But for those races without the tradition of self-management, 'let the secretaries do it' is the most common impression of secretaries, secretaries are perfect parental officials who can be relied on wholeheartedly, who can maintain a utopian life for them, far away from ambition and struggle, until the end of their life.",
      "defName": "SecretaryClone",
      "enabled": true,
      "name": "Secretary",
      "price": 10000
    },
